# Change Discipline

- Change only what is needed for the requested behavior.
- Preserve public interfaces unless the task requires a change.
- Avoid speculative abstractions, premature generalization and unnecessary dependencies.
- Do not rewrite a module just to match personal preferences.
- Keep formatting changes limited to touched code unless requested.
- Update related tests, types, docs and examples when behavior or contracts change.
- Explain any unavoidable scope expansion before proceeding.
